{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Machinery.DerivedCharacterCatalogue","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Machinery.DerivedCharacterCatalogue","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Rat.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanChiPerRep"],"declarations":80,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Phase2.figureEightTwoOneHiggsChiUnit_laurent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Phase2.figureEightTwoOneHiggsChiUnit_laurent","kind":"theorem","line":585,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L585-L591","doc":"The Figure-eight `(2,1)` character over `ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` is the Laurent\npolynomial `h⁴ + 2h² − 1`, `h = T − T⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Phase2.borromeanTwoOneBaryonChiUnit_laurent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Phase2.borromeanTwoOneBaryonChiUnit_laurent","kind":"theorem","line":578,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L578-L583","doc":"The Borromean `(2,1)` Kauffman character over the **non-field**\n`ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` is the Laurent polynomial `chi21_borromean (T² − T⁻²)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Phase2.figureEightTwoOneHiggsChiUnit_bar_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Phase2.figureEightTwoOneHiggsChiUnit_bar_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":561,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L561-L564","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Phase2.borromeanTwoOneBaryonChiUnit_bar_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Phase2.borromeanTwoOneBaryonChiUnit_bar_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":552,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L552-L559","doc":"Both reframed standard-irrep characters are **bar-invariant** (`q ↦ q⁻¹`\nfixes them): the bridge polynomials are even in their argument, and `q ↦\nq⁻¹` flips `H ↦ −H` / `h ↦ −h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Phase2.figureEightTwoOneHiggsChiUnit_eq_poly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Phase2.figureEightTwoOneHiggsChiUnit_eq_poly","kind":"theorem","line":539,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L539-L550","doc":"**Figure-eight `(2,1)` reframed** equals the even `R[h]` polynomial\n`h⁴ + 2h² − 1` at `h = ↑q − ↑q⁻¹`.  Division-free; sole input\n`↑q · ↑q⁻¹ = 1`.  Hence the cell's `χ^{(2,1)}` is a genuine `ℤ[q, q⁻¹]`\nLaurent polynomial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Phase2.figureEightTwoOneHiggsChiUnit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Phase2.figureEightTwoOneHiggsChiUnit","kind":"def","line":534,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L534-L537","doc":"Figure-eight `(2,1)` higgs, division-free palindromic Laurent over a unit:\n`q⁴ − 2q² + 1 − 2q⁻² + q⁻⁴`, with `1/q^k` replaced by `(↑q⁻¹)^k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Phase2.borromeanTwoOneBaryonChiUnit_eq_poly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Phase2.borromeanTwoOneBaryonChiUnit_eq_poly","kind":"theorem","line":517,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L517-L532","doc":"**Borromean `(2,1)` reframed** equals the faithful `R[h]` character\n`chi21_borromean` at `H = ↑q² − ↑q⁻²` (the Kauffman `t = q²`\nsubstitution).  Division-free; sole input `↑q · ↑q⁻¹ = 1`.  Hence the\ncell's `χ^{(2,1)}` is a genuine `ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` Laurent polynomial.\n(The `linear_combination` coefficient is the exact quotient of\n`qform − chi21_borromean(↑q²−↑q⁻²)` by `↑q·↑q⁻¹ − 1`, machine-derived.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Phase2.borromeanTwoOneBaryonChiUnit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Phase2.borromeanTwoOneBaryonChiUnit","kind":"def","line":510,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L510-L515","doc":"Borromean `(2,1)` baryon, division-free Kauffman Laurent over a unit `q`:\n`−q¹² + 3q⁸ − 3q⁴ + 4 − 3q⁻⁴ + 3q⁻⁸ − q⁻¹²`, division by `q^k` replaced by\n`(↑q⁻¹)^k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Phase2.cinquefoilOneOneMuonChiUnit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Phase2.cinquefoilOneOneMuonChiUnit","kind":"def","line":507,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L507-L508","doc":"Cinquefoil `(1,1)` muon, division-free: `−(↑q⁻¹)⁵`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Phase2.trefoilOneOneElectronChiUnit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Phase2.trefoilOneOneElectronChiUnit","kind":"def","line":504,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L504-L505","doc":"Trefoil `(1,1)` electron, division-free: `−(↑q⁻¹)³`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Phase2.hopfOneOneDiquarkChiUnit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Phase2.hopfOneOneDiquarkChiUnit","kind":"def","line":501,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L501-L502","doc":"Hopf `(1,1)` diquark, division-free: the sign-rep monomial `(↑q⁻¹)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Phase2.instIsRMatrixDerivedFigureEightTwoOneHiggs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Phase2.instIsRMatrixDerivedFigureEightTwoOneHiggs","kind":"instance","line":476,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L476-L479","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Phase2.figureEightTwoOneHiggsChi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Phase2.figureEightTwoOneHiggsChi","kind":"def","line":473,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L473-L474","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Phase2.figureEightTwoOneHiggs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Phase2.figureEightTwoOneHiggs","kind":"def","line":458,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L458-L471","doc":"Figure-eight `(2,1)` higgs-pion-half: palindromic\n`q⁴ − 2q² + 1 − 2q⁻² + q⁻⁴` from the R-matrix on V⊗³. Stored Laurent is\n`[(-4,1), (-2,-2), (0,1), (2,-2), (4,1)]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Phase2.instIsRMatrixDerivedFigureEightOneOneOneHiggs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Phase2.instIsRMatrixDerivedFigureEightOneOneOneHiggs","kind":"instance","line":453,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L453-L456","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Phase2.figureEightOneOneOneHiggsChi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Phase2.figureEightOneOneOneHiggsChi","kind":"def","line":451,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L451-L451","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Phase2.figureEightOneOneOneHiggs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Phase2.figureEightOneOneOneHiggs","kind":"def","line":438,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L438-L449","doc":"Figure-eight `(1,1,1)` higgs-pion-half: sign rep, also evaluates to `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Phase2.instIsRMatrixDerivedFigureEightThreeHiggs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Phase2.instIsRMatrixDerivedFigureEightThreeHiggs","kind":"instance","line":433,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L433-L436","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Phase2.figureEightThreeHiggsChi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Phase2.figureEightThreeHiggsChi","kind":"def","line":431,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L431-L431","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Phase2.figureEightThreeHiggs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Phase2.figureEightThreeHiggs","kind":"def","line":418,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L418-L429","doc":"Figure-eight `(3,)` higgs-pion-half: trivial rep, evaluates to `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Phase2.instIsRMatrixDerivedCinquefoilOneOneMuon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Phase2.instIsRMatrixDerivedCinquefoilOneOneMuon","kind":"instance","line":406,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L406-L409","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Phase2.cinquefoilOneOneMuonChi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Phase2.cinquefoilOneOneMuonChi","kind":"def","line":404,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L404-L404","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Phase2.cinquefoilOneOneMuon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Phase2.cinquefoilOneOneMuon","kind":"def","line":391,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L391-L402","doc":"Cinquefoil `(1,1)` muon: sign rep on σ_1⁵ gives `(−q⁻¹)⁵ = −q⁻⁵`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Phase2.instIsRMatrixDerivedCinquefoilTwoMuon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Phase2.instIsRMatrixDerivedCinquefoilTwoMuon","kind":"instance","line":386,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L386-L389","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Phase2.cinquefoilTwoMuonChi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Phase2.cinquefoilTwoMuonChi","kind":"def","line":384,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L384-L384","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Phase2.cinquefoilTwoMuon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Phase2.cinquefoilTwoMuon","kind":"def","line":371,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L371-L382","doc":"Cinquefoil `(2,)` muon: trivial rep on σ_1⁵ gives `q⁵`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Phase2.instIsRMatrixDerivedTrefoilOneOneElectron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Phase2.instIsRMatrixDerivedTrefoilOneOneElectron","kind":"instance","line":364,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L364-L367","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Phase2.trefoilOneOneElectronChi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Phase2.trefoilOneOneElectronChi","kind":"def","line":362,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L362-L362","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Phase2.trefoilOneOneElectron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Phase2.trefoilOneOneElectron","kind":"def","line":349,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L349-L360","doc":"Trefoil `(1,1)` electron: sign rep on σ_1³ gives `(−q⁻¹)³ = −q⁻³`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Phase2.instIsRMatrixDerivedTrefoilTwoElectron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Phase2.instIsRMatrixDerivedTrefoilTwoElectron","kind":"instance","line":344,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L344-L347","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Phase2.trefoilTwoElectronChi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Phase2.trefoilTwoElectronChi","kind":"def","line":342,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L342-L342","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Phase2.trefoilTwoElectron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Phase2.trefoilTwoElectron","kind":"def","line":329,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L329-L340","doc":"Trefoil `(2,)` electron: trivial rep on σ_1³ gives `q³`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Phase2.instIsRMatrixDerivedHopfOneOneDiquark","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Phase2.instIsRMatrixDerivedHopfOneOneDiquark","kind":"instance","line":322,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L322-L325","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Phase2.hopfOneOneDiquarkChi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Phase2.hopfOneOneDiquarkChi","kind":"def","line":320,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L320-L320","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Phase2.hopfOneOneDiquark","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Phase2.hopfOneOneDiquark","kind":"def","line":307,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L307-L318","doc":"Hopf `(1,1)` diquark: sign Hecke rep on σ_1² gives `(−q⁻¹)² = q⁻²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Phase2.instIsRMatrixDerivedHopfTwoDiquark","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Phase2.instIsRMatrixDerivedHopfTwoDiquark","kind":"instance","line":302,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L302-L305","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Phase2.hopfTwoDiquarkChi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Phase2.hopfTwoDiquarkChi","kind":"def","line":299,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L299-L300","doc":"The chi for Hopf `(2,)`: simply `q²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Phase2.hopfTwoDiquark","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Phase2.hopfTwoDiquark","kind":"def","line":286,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L286-L297","doc":"Hopf `(2,)` diquark: trivial Hecke rep on `T(2,2) = σ_1²`, giving `q²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.borromean_two_one_baryon_partition_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.borromean_two_one_baryon_partition_sum","kind":"theorem","line":258,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L258-L261","doc":"Sanity: the partition `[2, 1]` sums to the strand count `3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.borromean_two_one_baryon_kauffman","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.borromean_two_one_baryon_kauffman","kind":"theorem","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L254-L256","doc":"The Borromean / (2,1) / baryon cell uses the Kauffman convention. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.borromean_two_one_baryon_is_derived","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.borromean_two_one_baryon_is_derived","kind":"theorem","line":250,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L250-L252","doc":"The Borromean / (2,1) / baryon cell is tagged `derived`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.instIsRMatrixDerivedBorromeanTwoOneBaryon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.instIsRMatrixDerivedBorromeanTwoOneBaryon","kind":"instance","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L239-L246","doc":"The Borromean / (2,1) / baryon cell is R-matrix-derived. The instance\nis **fully discharged** (no `sorry`): `agrees` is the proven theorem\n`borromeanTwoOneBaryonChi_eq_t17`, with `rmatrixChi` set to the T17\nh-form in the Kauffman variable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.borromeanTwoOneBaryonChi_eq_t17","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.borromeanTwoOneBaryonChi_eq_t17","kind":"theorem","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L223-L237","doc":"**T17 is the first catalogue instance.** The stored Kauffman Laurent\nof the Borromean `(2,1)` cell equals T17's published h-form\n`2 − 3h⁴ − h⁶` evaluated at `q²` (the Kauffman `t = q²` substitution),\nfor every nonzero `q` in any field. The proof reuses T17's proven\nform-equivalence `chi21_borromean_qform_eq_hform`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.borromeanTwoOneBaryonChi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.borromeanTwoOneBaryonChi","kind":"def","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L216-L221","doc":"Genuine `ℚ → ℚ` evaluation of `borromeanTwoOneBaryon.chiLambdaQLaurent`\n(hand-transcribed from the cell's `(q_degree, coeff)` pairs\n`[(-12,-1),(-8,3),(-4,-3),(0,4),(4,-3),(8,3),(12,-1)]` to avoid string\nparsing in Lean — degrees are in the Kauffman variable `t = q²`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.borromeanTwoOneBaryon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.borromeanTwoOneBaryon","kind":"def","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L193-L214","doc":"The Borromean / (2,1) / baryon cell, recording T17's R-matrix\nderivation in Kauffman convention. The Laurent encoding\n`−q¹² + 3q⁸ − 3q⁴ + 4 − 3q⁻⁴ + 3q⁻⁸ − q⁻¹²` is the q-doubled form\nof the Kassel polynomial `χ⁽²,¹⁾(β_Bor) = 2 − 3h⁴ − h⁶` (with\nh = q − q⁻¹). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.IsLRFactorisedDerived.lrEquivalence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.IsLRFactorisedDerived.lrEquivalence","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L184-L184","doc":"The stored Laurent agrees with the LR-factorised character at every\nnonzero `q` (the LR-derivation certificate; was `True`). The instance is\ngated on the rigorous bridge-factor table for the deuteron base case. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.IsLRFactorisedDerived.lrFactorisedChi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.IsLRFactorisedDerived.lrFactorisedChi","kind":"def","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L180-L180","doc":"The LR-factorised character: parabolic restriction × LR\nmulti-coefficients × bridge factor `ω_{μ_p, μ_n, λ}(q)`, assembled into\na `q`-rational `R → R` function. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.IsLRFactorisedDerived.storedChi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.IsLRFactorisedDerived.storedChi","kind":"def","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L176-L176","doc":"A genuine `R → R` evaluation of the cell's stored `χ^λ` Laurent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.IsLRFactorisedDerived.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.IsLRFactorisedDerived.mk","kind":"ctor","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L173-L173","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.IsLRFactorisedDerived","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.IsLRFactorisedDerived","kind":"class","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L165-L184","doc":"A cell is LR-factorised-derived when its χ^λ was computed via the\nparabolic restriction + LR-multi-coefficient + bridge-factor `ω`\nformula. NEAR-MATCH tier; instance gated on Phase 1.1 of the Tier 1\nroadmap.\n\nMirrors the non-vacuous `IsRMatrixDerived` shape: the fields carry real\n`R → R` data (generic field `R`, §7c) and a real equality `Prop` — no\nlonger an opaque `True` marker. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.IsRMatrixDerived.agrees","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.IsRMatrixDerived.agrees","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L155-L155","doc":"The stored Laurent agrees with the R-matrix character at every\nnonzero `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.IsRMatrixDerived.rmatrixChi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.IsRMatrixDerived.rmatrixChi","kind":"def","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L152-L152","doc":"The categorical R-matrix character `χ^λ(β_K)` this cell realises,\nas a `q`-rational function (T17 template). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.IsRMatrixDerived.storedChi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.IsRMatrixDerived.storedChi","kind":"def","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L149-L149","doc":"A genuine `R → R` evaluation of the cell's stored Laurent\n`chiLambdaQLaurent` (in the Kauffman variable). Generic over a field\n`R` per §7c — no ordering / `Real.*` is involved, only the inverses\nthe Laurent needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.IsRMatrixDerived.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.IsRMatrixDerived.mk","kind":"ctor","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L144-L144","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.IsRMatrixDerived","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.IsRMatrixDerived","kind":"class","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L122-L155","doc":"A cell is R-matrix-derived when its stored `χ^λ` (as a genuine\n`ℚ → ℚ` Laurent evaluation, `storedChi`) agrees, away from `q = 0`,\nwith the categorical R-matrix character `rmatrixChi` obtained from the\nT17 template (R-matrix on `V⊗ⁿ` + Schur-Weyl projection to the\n`λ`-block + trace).\n\nThis is a genuine §3b-cond conditional class — its fields carry real\n`R → R` data (generic over a field `R`, §7c) and a real equality `Prop`,\nnot an opaque `True` marker.\nThe instance for `borromeanTwoOneBaryon` is **fully discharged** (no\n`sorry`): `agrees` is the proven theorem `borromeanTwoOneBaryonChi_eq_t17`,\nwhich reuses T17's `chi21_borromean_qform_eq_hform`.\n\nHONESTY (mirrors the `BorromeanChiPerRep.lean` scope note): the proven\ncontent is `storedChi = rmatrixChi` at the level of *q-rational forms*.\nThat `rmatrixChi` is itself the categorical R-matrix trace (rather than\njust the published h-polynomial) is, at the time of writing,\nNARRATIVE-ONLY for the seminormal Hecke-representation step — it is\nindependently confirmed numerically (≤ 4e-50) by\n`borromean_chi_independent_crosscheck.py`. The class therefore certifies\nthe catalogue cell against the *formalised* T17 polynomial, not against\nan in-Lean construction of the seminormal representation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.KnotPartitionAtomCell.derivationRef","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.KnotPartitionAtomCell.derivationRef","kind":"def","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L112-L112","doc":"Citation: commit-sha or audit-doc path of the structural derivation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.KnotPartitionAtomCell.tier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.KnotPartitionAtomCell.tier","kind":"def","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L110-L110","doc":"Provenance tier (see `Tier`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.KnotPartitionAtomCell.kLambda","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.KnotPartitionAtomCell.kLambda","kind":"def","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L108-L108","doc":"Per-partition truncation order `k_λ` per\n`prop:per-partition-k-lambda-rule`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.KnotPartitionAtomCell.qConvention","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.KnotPartitionAtomCell.qConvention","kind":"def","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L105-L105","doc":"Variable convention for `chiLambdaQLaurent`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.KnotPartitionAtomCell.chiLambdaQLaurent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.KnotPartitionAtomCell.chiLambdaQLaurent","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L103-L103","doc":"χ^λ(β_K)(q) as a Laurent in q: list of (q_degree, coefficient_string)\npairs. Negative q_degree allowed. Convention stored in `qConvention`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.KnotPartitionAtomCell.strandCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.KnotPartitionAtomCell.strandCount","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L100-L100","doc":"n_K, the strand count of the braid representative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.KnotPartitionAtomCell.braidWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.KnotPartitionAtomCell.braidWord","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L98-L98","doc":"Canonical braid word for K in B_{n_K}, as a pretty string. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.KnotPartitionAtomCell.atom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.KnotPartitionAtomCell.atom","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L96-L96","doc":"QOU atom / observable target (e.g. \"borromean-baryon\", \"5Li\"). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.KnotPartitionAtomCell.partition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.KnotPartitionAtomCell.partition","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L94-L94","doc":"Partition λ ⊢ n_K as a non-increasing list of positive ints. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.KnotPartitionAtomCell.knot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.KnotPartitionAtomCell.knot","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L92-L92","doc":"Knot operator name (from the PR #1677 census or atom-braid prefix). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.KnotPartitionAtomCell.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.KnotPartitionAtomCell.mk","kind":"ctor","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L90-L90","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.KnotPartitionAtomCell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.KnotPartitionAtomCell","kind":"structure","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L83-L112","doc":"A catalogue cell identifies a (knot K, partition λ, atom A) triple\nand stores the derived character data plus provenance.\n\nThis is the Lean schema mirror of the Python\n`KnotPartitionAtomCell` dataclass. Fields are kept as primitive types\n(strings, integer lists, etc.) so the schema can be ported across the\nPython/Lean boundary without bringing in heavy algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.instReprTier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.instReprTier","kind":"instance","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L79-L79","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.instReprTier.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.instReprTier.repr","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L79-L79","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.instDecidableEqTier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.instDecidableEqTier","kind":"instance","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L79-L79","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Tier.extracted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Tier.extracted","kind":"ctor","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L78-L78","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Tier.calAnchored","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Tier.calAnchored","kind":"ctor","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L77-L77","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Tier.derived","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Tier.derived","kind":"ctor","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L76-L76","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.Tier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.Tier","kind":"inductive","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L74-L79","doc":"Three provenance tiers per AGENTS.md `tier` discipline. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.instReprQConvention","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.instReprQConvention","kind":"instance","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L66-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.instReprQConvention.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.instReprQConvention.repr","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L66-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.instDecidableEqQConvention","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.instDecidableEqQConvention","kind":"instance","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L66-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QConvention.kassel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QConvention.kassel","kind":"ctor","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L65-L65","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QConvention.kauffman","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QConvention.kauffman","kind":"ctor","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L64-L64","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QConvention","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QConvention","kind":"inductive","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/DerivedCharacterCatalogue.lean#L62-L66","doc":"Two conventions for the catalogue's Laurent-in-q storage. ","signatureChunk":0}]}